From: MacRunner <noreply@macrunner.app>
Subject: [PATCH] toolchain: enable aarch64 PE arch for Wine host services

Symptom:
    After successful build, `wine wineboot` exited 0 silently and never
    populated drive_c. Investigation showed wineboot.exe was missing
    from engine/wine/dist. Configure marked programs/{wineboot, services,
    conhost, rpcss, plugplay, spoolsv, termsv, winemenubuilder, wuauserv}
    as DISABLED for both i386 and x86_64 archs.

Root cause:
    Wine 11 with the new WoW64 architecture compiles host system services
    as PE binaries matching HOST_ARCH. On Apple Silicon HOST_ARCH=aarch64,
    so without an aarch64 mingw toolchain, configure auto-disables those
    services. Homebrew `mingw-w64` ships only x86_64 and i386 wrappers.

Fix (no Wine source change — toolchain + configure flags):
    1. Bundle prebuilt llvm-mingw with aarch64-w64-mingw32-clang under
       engine/toolchain/llvm-mingw-20260505-ucrt-macos-universal/.
       Source: https://github.com/mstorsjo/llvm-mingw releases.

    2. scripts/build-wine.sh exports llvm-mingw bin at the END of PATH
       (so its `clang` does not shadow Apple clang for the host build)
       and pins CC=/usr/bin/clang, CXX=/usr/bin/clang++.

    3. configure switched from `--enable-archs=x86_64,i386` to
       `--enable-archs=aarch64,x86_64,i386`. Result:
           HOST_ARCH = aarch64
           PE_ARCHS  = aarch64 x86_64 i386
       wineboot, services, conhost et al. now build for aarch64 PE.

This is the toolchain piece needed for an arm64-native Wine host on
Apple Silicon. The x86_64/i386 PE remain (Windows .exe runs through
Rosetta 2 inside Wine).
